## 4. Generate a Safe Test Event

Use only your own lab machine.

If SSH is available locally, run:

```bash
ssh invalid-lab-user@localhost
```

If prompted, enter an incorrect password for a test account, or allow the invalid username attempt to fail.

Then inspect the logs:

```bash
sudo grep -Ei "Failed password|Invalid user" /var/log/auth.log | tail
```

You may see a message similar to:

```text
Failed password for invalid user invalid-lab-user from 127.0.0.1
```

The exact message depends on the SSH configuration and authentication method.

Do not run automated password-guessing tools or test against public systems for this exercise.

