## 5. Identify the Important Fields

When you find an authentication event, record:

| Field | What to identify |
|---|---|
| Timestamp | When did it happen? |
| Hostname | Which endpoint generated it? |
| Username | Which account was targeted? |
| Source IP | Where did the connection originate? |
| Event | Was it a failed or successful login? |
| Frequency | Were there repeated attempts? |

Example:

```text
Timestamp: 10:15:01
Hostname: ubuntu-lab
Username: invalid-lab-user
Source IP: 127.0.0.1
Event: Failed SSH authentication
```

These are illustrative values. Use the evidence from your own system.

