## 10. Check Related User and Process Activity

After identifying a suspicious authentication event, examine relevant endpoint evidence.

Show currently logged-in users:

```bash
who
```

Show login sessions and activity:

```bash
w
```

Review recent login history:

```bash
last -n 20
```

Review current processes:

```bash
ps aux
```

Review network connections:

```bash
sudo ss -tunap
```

These commands provide supporting context. They do not necessarily prove which process or person caused an earlier event, and some historical details may not be available.

